---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_TEL } from '../../../lib/site.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Arizona expansive soils and why drainage often matters more than steel"
  description="Expansive clay soils in Arizona shrink and swell with moisture. Controlling water is often the highest-leverage first step before any structural repair."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Arizona expansive soils and why drainage often matters more than steel</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Much of Arizona sits on expansive clay soils that shrink when dry and swell when wet. That movement shows up as cracks, sloping floors, and sticking doors.
    </p>

    <section>
      <p>
        Steel can stabilize a structure. It does not stop the soil from moving. If water is still being delivered to the clay (poor grading, clogged gutters, irrigation against the foundation, plumbing leaks), the same forces remain.
      </p>
      <p>
        In many cases the highest-leverage first step is controlling moisture: grading, drainage, gutters, and irrigation changes. Sometimes that is enough. Sometimes it is the necessary preparation before any structural work will hold.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ignoring drainage and going straight to piers is a common and expensive pattern.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Want to understand the moisture picture at your house?</strong></p>
        <a class="phone-link" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>{PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
